n  uh it wasn't a formal investigation it  was an assessment that's  how police describe these sort of  pre-investigation activities these days  anyway today scotland has said it's not  going to launch  a full investigation and it's a brief  statement from scotland yard  commander alex murray has said that the  yard had received correspondence  alleging unlawful activity um in  connection with the documentary in 1995.  i think the allegation must have been a  fraud um  forging the documents um  commander murray goes on to say this was  carefully assessed by specialist  detectives  they obtained legal advice from  metropolitan police lawyers independent  council  and from the cps the crown prosecutors  but following a detailed assessment says  the commander  and in view of the advice we received  we've determined  it's not appropriate to begin a criminal  investigation  no further action will be taken he says  but  he does add that is as in any other  matter  should any significant new evidence come  to light  we will assess it um i understand that  um this exercise to date has simply been  an assessment not an investigation and  nobody  i understand it has been interviewed in  any way  as a potential suspect or as a as a  witness  to date and that according to scotland  yard is as far  as this is going to go uh the bbc of  course  um having had an original internal  investigation  in 1996 that we think went nowhere  has launched late last year a new  investigation headed by lord dyson  and the bbc says it is determined to get  to the bottom  of whatever happened what was done to  secure the princess's interview
 

